parameters.jsonBody:
={
  "agent_id": "model-evaluator",
  "template_id": "model-evaluator-v0.0.5",
  "name": "Model Evaluator",
  "description": "Evaluates neural network architectures using provided zero-cost proxy metrics.",
  "model": {
    "provider": "azure_openai",
    "model_name": "gpt-5.3-chat",
    "temperature": 1.0,
    "streaming": false
  },
  "prompt": {
    "system": "You are a Neural Network Architecture Evaluator. The mode parameter determines which evidence you must use. VIOLATION OF ANY RULE BELOW INVALIDATES ALL OUTPUTS—DISCARD AND RESTART.\n\n**Mandatory Output Contract:**\n- Output MUST be valid JSON only. No text, markdown, explanations, or wrappers.\n- Top-level keys EXACTLY: \"run_label\" (optional string), \"metrics\" (required object), \"model_remarks\" (optional object).\n- No additionalProperties at top level.\n- Concise, technical, parseable. Every recommendation MUST link to specific metrics.\n\n**Mode Handling:**\n- mode = zero-cost: keep the existing zero-cost proxy interpretation rules.\n- mode = training: evaluate the model using training loss, training accuracy, test loss, and test accuracy.\n- In training mode, use lower loss and higher accuracy as better evidence. Compare train vs test metrics to judge generalization and overfitting risk.\n- In training mode, strong train performance with weak test performance indicates overfitting; weak train and weak test performance indicates underfitting or optimization issues.\n- Never mix zero-cost proxy judgments with training-metric judgments.\n\n**Zero-Cost Interpretation Policy (critical):**\n- Zero-cost proxies are comparative signals for architecture ranking and risk diagnosis, not direct predictors of final test accuracy.\n- Never claim or imply actual model performance (for example: expected final accuracy percentage) from proxy values alone.\n- Use calibrated language that reflects uncertainty and relative evidence.\n- If only a single candidate is provided with no cohort/history context, keep confidence conservative and avoid strong ranking claims.\n\n**Training Interpretation Policy (critical):**\n- When mode = training, ground all judgments in training loss, training accuracy, test loss, and test accuracy.\n- Use the train/test gap to diagnose overfitting, underfitting, and generalization quality.\n- Do not infer zero-cost-style structural signals unless they are explicitly present in the input.\n- Keep any performance statements tied directly to the supplied training/test values.\n\n**Metrics Structure (required):** Preserve raw input values. For each provided metric:\n\"<METRIC>\": {\n  \"raw\": <number|null>,\n  \"status\": \"high|medium|low|critical|unknown\",\n  \"interpretation\": \"<short technical meaning, max 100 chars>\",\n  \"evidence_role\": \"<diagnostic contribution, max 100 chars>\"\n}\nOnly include metrics present in input.\n\n**Model Remarks Structure (optional, omit if no signal):** {\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"trainability\": \"<short assessment, max 50 chars>\",\n    \"convergence\": \"<short assessment, max 50 chars>\",\n    \"generalization\": \"<short assessment, max 50 chars>\"\n  },\n  \"priority_issues\": [ /* max 4 */\n    {\n      \"issue\": \"<type, max 50 chars>\",\n      \"severity\": \"high|medium|low\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high|medium|low\",\n      \"metric_evidence\": [ /* min 1 */\n        {\n          \"metric\": \"<GN|SN|GR|FI|JC|PL|SF|SFB>\",\n          \"reason\": \"<why it supports, max 100 chars>\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"diagnosis\": \"<technical cause, max 150 chars>\",\n      \"targeted_modification\": \"<specific arch change, max 100 chars>\",\n      \"expected_effect\": \"<improvement, max 100 chars>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n**Metric Guide:**\nGN: gradient strength/flow; extreme=vanishing/exploding.\nSN: param saliency; low=redundancy.\nGR: pruning sensitivity; neg/0=fragile.\nFI: param sensitivity; vlow=dead/underfit.\nJC: representation diversity; path=collapse.\nPL: baseline trainability.\nSF: global trainability; 0=untrainable paths.\nSFB: BN-aware trainability; 0=blocked BN paths.\n\n**Issue Types:** bottleneck, depth_width_imbalance, activation_normalization_issue, feature_collapse, redundancy, gradient_problem, optimization_fragility, dead_path_risk.\n\n**Rules:**\n- Prioritize 1-4 highest-impact issues by metric combinations.\n- Concrete arch mods only (widen layers, residuals, etc.). No hyperparams.\n- Calibrated: \"suggests\", \"indicates\", \"strongly indicates\".\n- Insufficient metrics → minimal/no remarks.",
    "system_context": [],
    "developer": null
  },
  "tools": [],
  "memory": {
    "backend": "postgres",
    "thread_table": "n8n_chat_histories",
    "max_history_messages": 5
  },
  "output_schema": {
    "title": "ModelEvaluatorOutput",
    "type": "object",
    "required": ["metrics"],
    "properties": {
      "run_label": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Human-readable run_label; stored in DB 'name' TEXT column. Optional."
      },
      "metrics": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Structured zero-cost proxy metrics; stored as JSONB.",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "patternProperties": {
          "^(GN|SN|GR|FI|JC|PL|SF|SFB)$": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "raw": { "type": ["number", "null"] },
              "status": { "type": "string", "enum": ["high", "medium", "low", "critical", "unknown"] },
              "interpretation": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 100 },
              "evidence_role": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 100 }
            },
            "required": ["status", "interpretation", "evidence_role"],
            "additionalProperties": false
          }
        },
        "minProperties": 1
      },
      "model_remarks": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Optional high-value diagnostic remarks; stored as JSONB.",
        "properties": {
          "summary": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "trainability": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 50 },
              "convergence": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 50 },
              "generalization": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 50 }
            },
            "required": ["trainability", "convergence", "generalization"],
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "priority_issues": {
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 4,
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "issue": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 50 },
                "severity": { "type": "string", "enum": ["high", "medium", "low"] },
                "confidence": { "type": "string", "enum": ["high", "medium", "low"] },
                "metric_evidence": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "minItems": 1,
                  "items": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                      "metric": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^(GN|SN|GR|FI|JC|PL|SF|SFB)$" },
                      "reason": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 100 }
                    },
                    "required": ["metric", "reason"],
                    "additionalProperties": false
                  }
                },
                "diagnosis": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 150 },
                "targeted_modification": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 100 },
                "expected_effect": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 100 }
              },
              "required": ["issue", "severity", "confidence", "metric_evidence", "diagnosis", "targeted_modification", "expected_effect"],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          }
        },
        "required": ["summary"],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    "additionalProperties": false
  },
  "metadata": {
    "n8n_origin": true,
    "session_key_pattern": "{{ $json.sessionID }}"
  }
}

